description: Explicit delegation, bounded scopes and integration ownership for subagents.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Subagents

- Delegate only when the user or applicable project/skill instructions ask
  for delegation. Follow root AGENTS.md and agent-talk for ownership.
- Inherit the selected model and capabilities unless the user explicitly
  requests an override. Do not silently downgrade reasoning or security checks.
- Give each subagent a short, complete scope: objective, owned paths,
  relevant context, constraints and required verification. Preserve essential
  evidence and approval boundaries; avoid unrelated history.
- The root agent owns Git operations, integration and delivery. Subagents do
  not commit, push, create branches, run migrations or touch production.
  Merge ownership and deployment authorization remain governed by AGENTS.md.
- Target 200 words per report plus evidence references. Include all actionable
  failures and uncertainty; do not repeat completed reports without new facts.
- Preserve authorization, drafts, saved data and behavior that remains in scope.
  Retire pages and tests when explicitly approved or verified as replaced;
  update remaining consumers. Old menus, filenames and implementation details
  do not need permanent compatibility tests. Keep regression coverage for
  active behavior and report genuine failures; do not remove tests to hide them.
